  "chapter": {
    "number": 35,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(36) For the end, by David the servant of the Lord."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The transgressor, that he may sin, says within himself, that there is no fear of God before his eyes.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For he has dealt craftily before him,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 66
          },
          {
            "text": "to discover his iniquity and hate it.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The words of his mouth are transgression and deceit: he is not inclined to understand how to do good.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He devises iniquity on his bed; he gives himself to every evil way; and does not abhor evil.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord, your mercy is in the heaven; and your truth reaches to the clouds.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Your righteousness is as the",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 67
          },
          {
            "text": "mountains of God, your judgments are as a great deep: O Lord, you will preserve men and beasts.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "How have you multiplied your mercy, O God! so the children of men shall trust in the shelter of your wings.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They shall be",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 68
          },
          {
            "text": "fully satisfied with the fatness of your house; and you shall cause them to drink of the full stream of your delights.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For with you is the fountain of life: in your light we shall see light.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Extend your mercy to them that know you; and your righteousness to the upright in heart.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let not the foot of pride come against me, and let not the hand of sinners move me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "There have all the workers of iniquity fallen: they are cast out, and shall not be able to stand.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 66,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "q. d. with regard to the discovering.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 35,
          "verse": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 67,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Or, vast mountains.",
        "reference": {
